\n\
**My board:** 4 creatures (2 Drakes, Ironroot Warlord 4/5, Sage's Row Savant 2/1), 7 untapped lands, and I drew Talrand!\n\
\n\
**Key decisions:**\n\
1. Cast Talrand ({2}{U}{U}) — 4 mana, leaves me with 3 lands untapped. Then every instant/sorcery makes a Drake!\n\
2. Should I attack Chandra? She's at 1 loyalty — any single Drake kills her. But opponent has Young Pyromancer and Boggart Brute for blocking ground creatures.\n\
\n\
**Plan:** Cast Talrand first (4 mana), then go to combat. Attack Chandra with 1 Drake (she dies at 1 loyalty), attack opponent with the other Drake for 2. Ironroot Warlord can't profitably attack into Boggart Brute + Young Pyromancer unless I want to trade.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — I have 7 untapped lands. If I cast Talrand ({2}{U}{U} = 4 mana), I have 3 left. That's enough for Befuddle ({2}{U})! So I can cast Talrand AND hold up Befuddle. And if I cast Befuddle, Talrand triggers and makes a Drake token! Beautiful.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Talrand.",
