I'd need {3}{G}{W}. I can get {G} from Thriving Isle... but it's tapped. I can get any color from Rupture Spire ({W}) and Prophetic Prism ({1}, {T}: any color = {G}). So: 3 Islands for {3}, Rupture Spire for {W}, and Prophetic Prism (needs {1} to activate) for {G} — that's actually 3+1+1+1 = 6 mana sources. Let me check: {3}{G}{W} = 5 total mana. I need to pay {1} to activate Prophetic Prism, so that costs 2 mana sources for 1 colored mana. Total: 3 Islands (for {3}) + 1 Island (to activate Prism) + Prism (for {G}) + Rupture Spire (for {W}) = 6 sources for 5 mana. That works!\n\
\n\
But is it worth it? Making a 1/1 Soldier means Ironroot goes to 7/5 and I have 7 creatures. I'm already attacking for lethal (16 damage vs 8 life). The only reason to activate would be insurance against removal. But it uses almost all my mana, leaving me unable to respond to anything.\n\
\n\
Actually, I'm already presenting way more than lethal. Let me just go to combat. If they kill one creature, I still have more than enough. Saving mana for Prophetic Prism's fixing ability or holding open mana seems fine.",
